# The Network: iCloud content
#
# Expects DIRECT. Lives in the overlay so the content plane stays direct whatever policy the panel hangs the company-wide Platforms/Apple.list on.
#
# The MMCS content service behind iMessage attachments, Photos, Drive and Backup. Proxied, the global block-quic setting rejected its HTTP/3 and the fallbacks inherited the proxy path's instability: 35 blocked attachment transfers in one 6.6 minute window on 2026-08-12, images stalling on the phone that sent them.
#
# This file carries names only. The content edges are also reached over HTTP/3 with no SNI the gateway can read, and those flows can only match by address; Platforms/Apple.list carries Apple's address space for them, after the named exceptions, because an address rule would otherwise take a flow that arrived by address with an SNI the exceptions own.

DOMAIN,content.icloud.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,icloud-content.com
DOMAIN-WILDCARD,p*-content.icloud.com
